<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Predicting independent event outcomes for local weather and football leagues</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The meteorological department forecasts that the probability of heavy rain in <b>{@city@}</b> this Saturday is <b>{@A_str@}</b>. Independently, the probability that the local football team, <b>{@team@}</b>, wins their weekend league match is <b>{@B_str@}</b>.</p>
<p>Let \(R\) be the event "it rains" and \(W\) be the event "the team wins". Because the weather does not affect the team's preparedness, assume \(R\) and \(W\) are <b>independent events</b>.</p>

<p><b>a) </b> Find the probability that it rains AND the team wins.</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as a fully simplified fraction or exact decimal).</i></p>
<p>\(P(R \text{ and } W) =\) [[input:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><b>b)  </b> Find the probability that it rains OR the team wins.</p>
<p>\(P(R \text{ or } W) =\) [[input:ans2]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>

<p><b>c) </b> Find the probability that it does NOT rain AND the team does NOT win.</p>
<p>\(P =\) [[input:ans3]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part a: Intersection</b><br>
Because the events are independent, the probability of both happening is the product of their individual probabilities:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(R \text{ and } W) = P(R) \times P(W) \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(R \text{ and } W) = {@A_str@} \times {@B_str@} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P(R \text{ and } W) = {@ta1@} } \)</p>

<p><b>Part b: Union</b><br>
Using the general addition rule, we add the individual probabilities and subtract the intersection:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(R \text{ or } W) = P(R) + P(W) - P(R \text{ and } W) \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(R \text{ or } W) = {@A_str@} + {@B_str@} - {@ta1@} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P(R \text{ or } W) = {@ta2@} } \)</p>

<p><b>Part c: Neither Event</b><br>
The event "neither happens" is the complement of the event "at least one happens" (the union).</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(\text{neither}) = 1 - P(R \text{ or } W) \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(\text{neither}) = 1 - {@ta2@} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P(\text{neither}) = {@ta3@} } \)</p>
<p><i>(Alternatively, you could multiply the independent complements: \(P(R') \times P(W') = (1 - {@A_str@}) \times (1 - {@B_str@}) = {@ta3@}\)).</i></p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
